# Dockerization and Deployment to DeanOS

This plan outlines the steps to dockerize the `evaiteclabs` project and deploy it to the `DeanOS` server, exposing it on port 3001.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] backend

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/projects/evaiteclabs/server.js)
- Change default `PORT` from 3000 to 3001.

#### [NEW] [Dockerfile](file:///c:/projects/evaiteclabs/Dockerfile)
- Create a lightweight Node.js Dockerfile to serve the static content using [server.js](file:///c:/projects/evaiteclabs/server.js).

#### [NEW] [docker-compose.yml](file:///c:/projects/evaiteclabs/docker-compose.yml)
- Define the service, build context, and port mapping (3001:3001).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `docker compose up -d` locally to verify the build and container startup.
- Check accessibility via `curl http://localhost:3001`.

### Manual Verification
- SSH into `DeanOS` and verify the deployment.
- Verify the website is accessible on the network at `http://deanos.local:3001`.
